helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155553	46			0	tr	Type the character that you want to separate the chapter number(s) from the caption number in the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Separator\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3155586	40			0	tr	In the \<emph\>Caption\</emph\> dialog, click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\captions_numbers.xhp	0	help	par_id3147226	43			0	tr	$[officename] can automatically add a caption when you insert an object, graphic, or table. Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - AutoCaption\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
