helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	bm_id3146875				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>headers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers; inserting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing from selection\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>new page styles from selection\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	hd_id3146875	21			0	tr	\<variable id=\"change_header\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/change_header.xhp\" name=\"Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\"\>Creating a Page Style Based on the Current Page\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153584	22			0	tr	You can design a page layout and then create a page style based on it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3154245	24			0	tr	For example, you can create a page style that displays a particular header, and another page style that displays a different header.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150503	26			0	tr	Open a new text document, choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\>, and then click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3150532	27			0	tr	Click the \<emph\>New Style from Selection\</emph\> icon and select \<emph\>New Styles from Selection\</emph\> from the submenu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153153	31			0	tr	Type a name for the page in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style name\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3153184	32			0	tr	Double-click the name in the list to apply the style to the current page. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155541	33			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and choose the new page style from the list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155572	34			0	tr	Type the text that you want in the header. Position the cursor into the main text area outside of the header.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3155592	25			0	tr	\<emph\>Dosya - Yazdır\</emph\> seçeneğini seçin.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147771	28			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page break\</item\> and then select “Default” from the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\change_header.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810	29			0	tr	Repeat steps 2-6 to create a second custom page style with a different header.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Bölüm numaralaması				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147682				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>outlines;numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>deleting;heading numbers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter numbering\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headings; numbering/paragraph styles\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>numbering;headings\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147682	22			0	tr	\<variable id=\"chapter_numbering\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/chapter_numbering.xhp\" name=\"Outline Numbering\"\>Outline Numbering\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155605	23			0	tr	You can modify the heading hierarchy or assign a level in the hierarchy to a custom paragraph style. You can also add chapter and section numbering to heading paragraph styles. By default, the "Heading 1" paragraph style is at the top of the outline hierarchy.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155626	35			0	tr	To Add Automatic Numbering to a Heading Style				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	36			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155891	37			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Paragraph Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the heading style that you want to add chapter numbers to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513	25			0	tr	In the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbers\</item\> box, select the numbering style that you want to use, and then click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>OK\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107CE				0	tr	To Remove Automatic Outline Numbering From a Heading Paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D5				0	tr	Click at the beginning of the text in the heading paragraph, after the number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_idN107D9				0	tr	Press the \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Backspace\</item\> key to delete the number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155552	26			0	tr	To Use a Custom Paragraph Style as a Heading				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3155571	38			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Numbering\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147758	27			0	tr	Select the custom style in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147782	39			0	tr	Click the heading level that you want to assign to the custom paragraph style in the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Level\</item\> list. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\chapter_numbering.xhp	0	help	par_id3147808	28			0	tr	\<emph\>Sil\</emph\>'e tıklayın.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Conditional Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155619				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>matching conditional text in fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>if-then queries as fields\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text; setting up\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>text; conditional text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining;conditions\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155619	4			0	tr	\<variable id=\"conditional_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text\"\>Conditional Text\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155879	5			0	tr	You can set up fields in your document that display text when a condition that you define is met. For example, you can define the conditional text that is displayed in a series of reminder letters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155895	6			0	tr	Setting up conditional text in this example is a two-part process. First you create a variable, and then you create the condition.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153175	61			0	tr	To Define a Conditional Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153185	62			0	tr	The first part of the example is to define a variable for the condition statement. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155566	8			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Variables\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147759	9			0	tr	Click "Set variable" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147784	10			0	tr	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3147810	57			0	tr	Click "Text" in the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\> list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id7748344				0	tr	Enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, and then click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\>.\<br/\>The Format list now displays a "General" format.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145645	63			0	tr	To Define a Condition and the Conditional Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145659	64			0	tr	The second part of the example is to define the condition that must be met, and to insert a placeholder for displaying the conditional text in your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151193	12			0	tr	Place the cursor where you want to insert the conditional text in your text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151212	65			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3151250	13			0	tr	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155936	14			0	tr	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Reminder EQ "3"\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\>               \<emph/\>box. In other words, the conditional text will be displayed when the variable in the field that you defined in the first part of this example is equal to three.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155969	15			0	tr	The quotation marks enclosing the "3" indicate that the variable that you defined in the first part of this example is a text string.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150446	16			0	tr	Type the text that you want to display when the condition is met in the \<emph\>Then\</emph\> box. There is almost no limit to the length of the text that you can enter. You can paste a paragraph into this box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150473	17			0	tr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155073	66			0	tr	To Display the Conditional Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155086	67			0	tr	In this example, the conditional text is displayed when the value of the conditional variable is equal to 3.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155110	19			0	tr	Place your cursor in front of the field that you defined in the first part of this example, and then choose \<emph\>Edit - Fields\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155136	68			0	tr	Replace the number in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\>               \<emph/\>box with 3, and then click\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155168	20			0	tr	If the field does not automatically update, press F9.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145714				0	tr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/02/14020000.xhp\" name=\"List of conditional operators\"\>List of conditional operators\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Conditional Text for Page Counts				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153108				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>page counts\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>conditional text;page counts\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153108	1			0	tr	\<variable id=\"conditional_text2\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/conditional_text2.xhp\" name=\"Conditional Text for Page Counts\"\>Conditional Text for Page Counts\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156228	3			0	tr	You can create a conditional text field that displays the word "pages" instead of "page" in conjunction with a page count field if your document contains more than one page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3156257	4			0	tr	Place the cursor in your document where you want to insert the page count.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150513	5			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Page Count\</item\>, and then enter a space.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	6			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\>, and then click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Functions\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3153166	9			0	tr	Click "Conditional text" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145256	7			0	tr	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page > 1\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145280	10			0	tr	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Pages\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Then\</item\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3145305	11			0	tr	Type \<item type=\"literal\"\>Page\</item\> in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Else\</item\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\conditional_text2.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	8			0	tr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
