helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	About Headers and Footers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155863				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>headers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;about\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>HTML documents; headers and footers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155863	38			0	tr	\<variable id=\"header_footer\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_footer.xhp\" name=\"About Headers and Footers\"\>About Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154255	35			0	tr	Headers and footers are areas in the top and the bottom page margins, where you can add text or graphics. Headers and footers are added to the current page style. Any page that uses the same style automatically receives the header or footer that you add. You can insert \<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04090000.xhp\" name=\"Fields\"\>Fields\</link\>, such as page numbers and chapter headings, in headers and footers in a text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150511	44			0	tr	The page style for the current page is displayed in the \<emph\>Status Bar\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896	39			0	tr	To add a header to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Header\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147119	43			0	tr	To add a footer to a page, choose \<emph\>Insert - Footer\</emph\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153726	40			0	tr	You can also choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\> or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab, and then select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\>               \<emph/\>or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer on\</item\>. Clear the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Same content left/right\</item\> check box if you want to define different headers and footers for even and odd pages.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3146876	36			0	tr	To use different headers or footers in your document, you must add them to different \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>, and then apply the styles to the pages where you want the headers or footer to appear.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150704	41			0	tr	Headers and Footers in HTML Documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3150717	34			0	tr	Some of the header and footer options are also available for HTML documents. Headers and footers are not supported by HTML and instead are exported with special tags, so that they can be viewed in a browser. Headers and footers are only exported in HTML documents if they are enabled in Web Layout mode. When you reopen the document in $[officename], the headers and footers are displayed correctly, including any fields that you inserted. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_footer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153174				0	tr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Page Styles\"\>Page Styles\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Defining Different Headers and Footers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155920				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>headers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;defining for left and right pages\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>page styles; changing\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>defining; headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>mirrored page layout\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155920	25			0	tr	\<variable id=\"header_pagestyles\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_pagestyles.xhp\" name=\"Defining Different Headers and Footers\"\>Defining Different Headers and Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3154263	26			0	tr	You can use different headers and footers on different pages in your document, so long as the pages use different page styles. $[officename] provides several predefined page styles, such as \<emph\>First page\</emph\>, \<emph\>Left page\</emph\> and \<emph\>Right page\</emph\>, or you can create a custom page style.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147105	27			0	tr	You can also use the mirrored page layout if you want to add a header to a page style that has different inner and outer page margins. To apply this option to a page style, choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>, click the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page\</item\> tab, and in the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Layout settings\</item\> area, choose “Mirrored” in the\<emph/\>         \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page layout\</item\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150224	28			0	tr	For example, you can use page styles to define different headers for even and odd pages in a document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150929	29			0	tr	Open a new text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150946	31			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Styles and Formatting\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Page Styles\</emph\> icon in the Styles and Formatting window.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510	30			0	tr	Right-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150536	33			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750	34			0	tr	Select\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146865	35			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select "Left Page".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3146889	36			0	tr	\<emph\>Sil\</emph\>'e tıklayın.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150714	37			0	tr	In the \<emph\>Styles and Formatting\</emph\> window, right-click "Left Page" in the list of page styles and choose \<emph\>Modify\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3150748	38			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Page Styles\</item\> dialog, click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3153172	39			0	tr	Select\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header on\</item\> and click the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Organizer\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147061	40			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Next Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select "Right Page".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3147086	41			0	tr	\<emph\>Sil\</emph\>'e tıklayın.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145263	42			0	tr	Double-click "Right Page" in the list of page styles to apply the style to the current page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_pagestyles.xhp	0	help	par_id3145284	43			0	tr	Enter text or graphics in the header for the Left Page style. After the next page is added to your document, enter text or graphics in the header for the Right Page style. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155919				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>running titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>floating titles in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers; chapter information\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>names; chapter names in headers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155919	3			0	tr	\<variable id=\"header_with_chapter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_chapter.xhp\" name=\"Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\"\>Inserting a Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153414	22			0	tr	Before you can insert chapter information into a header or footer, you must first set the outline numbering options for the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154244	23			0	tr	To Create a Paragraph Style for Chapter Titles				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155874	24			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155898	25			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Style\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, select the paragraph style that you want to use for chapter titles, for example, "Heading 1".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147124	26			0	tr	Select the numbering style for the chapter titles in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Number\</item\>               \<emph/\>box, for example, "1,2,3...".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150219	27			0	tr	Type "Chapter" followed by a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Before\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150245	28			0	tr	Enter a space in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>After\</item\>               \<emph/\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150949	29			0	tr	\<emph\>Sil\</emph\>'e tıklayın.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150505	30			0	tr	To Insert the Chapter Name and Number in a Header or a Footer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150527	5			0	tr	Apply the paragraph style that you defined for chapter titles to the chapter headings in your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153729	6			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Header\</item\>               \<emph/\>or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Footer\</item\>, and then select the page style for the current page from the submenu.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153762	7			0	tr	Click in the header or footer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146863	9			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Fields - Other\</item\> and click the\<emph/\>               \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Document\</item\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153175	10			0	tr	Click "Chapter" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Type\</item\>               \<emph/\>list and "Chapter number and name" in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format\</item\>               \<emph/\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147065	11			0	tr	Click \<emph\>Insert\</emph\> and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_chapter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147095	12			0	tr	The header on every page that uses the current page style automatically displays the chapter name and number.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Formatting Headers or Footers				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154866				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>inserting;lines under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>lines; under headers/above footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>headers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>footers;formatting\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>shadows;headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>borders;for headers/footers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154866	20			0	tr	\<variable id=\"header_with_line\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/header_with_line.xhp\" name=\"Formatting Headers or Footers\"\>Formatting Headers or Footers\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3154243	21			0	tr	You can apply direct formatting to the text in a header or footer. You can also adjust the spacing of the text relative to the header or footer frame or apply a border to the header or footer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3155873	22			0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Format - Page\</item\>               \<emph/\>and select the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Header\</item\>               \<emph/\>or \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Footer\</item\>               \<emph/\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147109	27			0	tr	Set the spacing options that you want to use.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3147128	23			0	tr	To add a border or a shadow to the header or the footer, click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>More\</item\>. The \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Border/Background\</item\>               \<emph/\>dialog opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3150520	24			0	tr	To add a separator line between the header or the footer and the content of the page, click the bottom edge of the square in the \<emph\>Line arrangement\</emph\> area. Click a line style in the \<emph\>Style\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\header_with_line.xhp	0	help	par_id3153742	25			0	tr	To adjust the spacing between the content of the header or footer and the line, clear the \<emph\>Synchronize\</emph\> box, and then enter a value in the\<emph\> Bottom\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Hiding Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148856				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>text; hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>sections;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>paragraphs;hiding\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>hiding;text, with conditions\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>variables;for hiding text\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148856	1			0	tr	\<variable id=\"hidden_text\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hidden_text.xhp\" name=\"Hiding Text\"\>Hiding Text\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3150103	2			0	tr	You can use fields and sections to hide or display text in your document if a condition is met.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153409	19			0	tr	Before you can hide text, you must first create a variable to use in the condition for hiding the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id5174108				0	tr	To Create a Variable				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153131	20			0	tr	Click in your document and choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149640	21			0	tr	Click the \<emph\>Variables \</emph\>tab and click "Set Variable" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149970	22			0	tr	Click "General" in the \<emph\>Format \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149620	23			0	tr	Type a name for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Name\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149869	24			0	tr	Enter a value for the variable in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Value\</item\> box, for example, \<item type=\"literal\"\>1\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145108	25			0	tr	To hide the variable in your document, select \<emph\>Invisible\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149585	26			0	tr	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156245	27			0	tr	To Hide Text				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145391	28			0	tr	Click in the document where you want to add the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3145409	5			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155325	29			0	tr	Click "Hidden Text" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154404	30			0	tr	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153371	31			0	tr	Type the text that you want to hide in the \<emph\>Hidden text \</emph\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154233	32			0	tr	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154256	33			0	tr	To Hide a Paragraph				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154853	34			0	tr	Click in the paragraph where you want to add the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3154872	35			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Fields - Other\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Functions \</emph\>tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155902	6			0	tr	Click "Hidden Paragraph" in the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>list.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3155947	36			0	tr	Enter a statement in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3149991	37			0	tr	Click \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert\</item\> and \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Close\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3793450				0	tr	You must enable this feature by removing the check mark from menu \<emph\>View - Hidden Paragraphs\</emph\>. When the check mark is set, you cannot hide any paragraph.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148675	38			0	tr	To Hide a Section				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148697	39			0	tr	Select the text that you want to hide in your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3153019	9			0	tr	\<emph\>Dosya - Yazdır\</emph\> seçeneğini seçin.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hidden_text.xhp	0	help	par_id3148950	40			0	tr	In the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\> area, select \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Hide\</item\>, and then enter an expression in the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Condition\</item\> box. For example, using the variable you previously defined, enter \<item type=\"literal\"\>Hide==1\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
