helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155845				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>hyperlinks; inserting from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>inserting; hyperlinks from Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>cross-references; inserting with Navigator\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>Navigator;inserting hyperlinks\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155845	21			0	tr	\<variable id=\"hyperlinks\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyperlinks.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\"\>Inserting Hyperlinks With the Navigator\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3155858	20			0	tr	You can insert a cross-reference as a hyperlink in your document using the Navigator. You can even cross-reference items from other \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\> documents. If you click the hyperlink when the document is opened in \<item type=\"productname\"\>%PRODUCTNAME\</item\>, you are taken to the cross-referenced item.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149833	32			0	tr	Open the document(s) containing the items you want to cross-reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3148846	23			0	tr	On the Standard bar, click the \<emph\>Navigator\</emph\> icon.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108	25			0	tr	Click the arrow next to the \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Drag Mode\</item\> icon, and ensure that \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert as Hyperlink\</item\>               \<emph/\>is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153396	31			0	tr	In the list at the bottom of the Navigator, select the document containing the item that you want to cross-reference.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153416	24			0	tr	In the Navigator list, click the plus sign next to the item that you want to insert as a hyperlink.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3153133	26			0	tr	Drag the item to where you want to insert the hyperlink in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyperlinks.xhp	0	help	par_id3149635	27			0	tr	The name of the item is inserted in the document as an underlined hyperlink.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149695				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>hyphenation;preventing for specific words\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>words;wrapping/not wrapping in text\</bookmark_value\>      \<bookmark_value\>switching off;hyphenation for specific words\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149695	20			0	tr	\<variable id=\"hyphen_prevent\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/hyphen_prevent.xhp\" name=\"Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words\"\>Preventing Hyphenation of Specific Words\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id5640125				0	tr	If your text is \<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/using_hyphen.xhp\"\>automatically hyphenated\</link\> and certain hyphenated words look ugly, or if you want specific words never to be hyphenated you can switch off hyphenation for those words:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153634	40			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Writing Aids\</emph\>            				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3153658	41			0	tr	Select a dictionary in the \<emph\>User-defined dictionary \</emph\>list, and then click \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147125	43			0	tr	If the list is empty, click \<emph\>New\</emph\> to create a dictionary.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150218	42			0	tr	In the\<emph\> Word\</emph\> box, type the word you want to exclude from hyphenation, followed by an equal sign (=), for example, "pretentious=".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3150247	65			0	tr	Click \<emph\>New\</emph\>, and then click \<emph\>Close\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3147036	29			0	tr	To quickly exclude a word from hyphenation, select the word, choose \<emph\>Format - Character\</emph\>, click the \<emph\>Font \</emph\>tab, and select "None" in the \<emph\>Language \</emph\>box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262761				0	tr	Some words contain special characters that %PRODUCTNAME treats as a hyphen. If you do not want such words to be hyphenated, you can insert a special code that prevents hyphenation at the position where the special code is inserted. Proceed as follows:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262850				0	tr	Enable the special features of complex text layout (CTL) languages: Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - Language Settings - Languages\</item\> and check \<emph\>Enabled for complex text layout (CTL)\</emph\>. Click OK.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262837				0	tr	Position the cursor at the place where no hyphenation should occur.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910262867				0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Formatting Mark - No-width no break\</item\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id0302200910572128				0	tr	Once the special character is inserted, you might disable CTL again. Support of CTL was only necessary to insert the special character.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\hyphen_prevent.xhp	0	help	par_id3154361	46			0	tr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/05030200.xhp\" name=\"Text Flow\"\>Text Flow\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
