helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149689	4			0	tr	\<variable id=\"indices_enter\"\>\<link href=\"text/swriter/guide/indices_enter.xhp\" name=\"Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\"\>Defining Index or Table of Contents Entries\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155862	6			0	tr	To Define Index Entries				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3156380	7			0	tr	Click in a word, or select the words in your document that you want to use as an index entry.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147409	9			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Entry\</emph\>, and do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153417	11			0	tr	To change the text that appears in the index, type the text that you want in the \<emph\>Entry\</emph\> box. The text that you type here does not replace the selected text in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3154258	8			0	tr	To add an index mark to similar words in your document, select \<emph\>Apply to all similar texts\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155889	10			0	tr	To add the entries to a custom index, click the \<emph\>New User-defined Index\</emph\> icon, enter the name of the index, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147119	12			0	tr	To Define Table of Contents Entries				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3147132	5			0	tr	The best way to generate a table of contents is to apply the predefined heading paragraph styles, such as "Heading 1", to the paragraphs that you want to include in your table of contents.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150230	13			0	tr	To Use a Custom Paragraph Style as a Table of Contents Entry				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150933	14			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Tools - Outline Numbering\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Numbering\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150964	15			0	tr	Select the paragraph style that you want to include in your table of contents in the \<emph\>Paragraph Style\</emph\> box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3150523	16			0	tr	In the \<emph\>Level\</emph\> list, click the hierarchical level that you want to apply the paragraph style to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\indices_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3153730	17			0	tr	Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. You can now apply the style to headings in your document and include them in your table of contents. 				20130618 17:22:18
