helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149641	44			0	tr	The wildcard for a single character is a period (.).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3153136	43			0	tr	The wildcard for zero or more occurrences of the previous character is an asterisk. For example: "123*" finds "12" "123", and "1233".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149609	45			0	tr	The wildcard combination to search for zero or more occurrences of any character is a period and asterisk (.*).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\guide\search_regexp.xhp	0	help	par_id3149854	46			0	tr	The wildcard for the end of a paragraph is a dollar sign ($). The wildcard character combination for the start of a paragraph is a caret and a period (^.).				20130618 17:22:18
