helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120229.xhp	0	help	par_id3143283	8			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_AUTH_FIELD_AUTHORITY_TYPE\"\>Select the source for the bibliography entry.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120229.xhp	0	help	par_id3147091	12			0	tr	\<link href=\"text/swriter/01/04120227.xhp\" name=\"Formatting bibliography entries\"\>Formatting bibliography entries\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Uyumluluk dosyasını düzenle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148768				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>editing; concordance files\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>concordance files; definition\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148768	1			0	tr	Uyumluluk dosyasını düzenle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151180	2			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_DLG_CREATE_AUTOMARK\"\>Create or edit a list of words to include in an Alphabetical Index.\</ahelp\> A concordance file lists words that should be referenced in an alphabetical index, together with the page number(s) where they appear in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id837427				0	tr	You can use the Find All button on the Find & Replace dialog to highlight all places where a word appears, then open the Insert Index Entry dialog to add that word and places to the alphabetical index. However, if you need the same set of alphabetical indexes in multiple documents, the concordance file allows to enter every word just once, then use the list many times.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154645	19			0	tr	To access the Edit Concordance File dialog:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149292	20			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Indexes and Tables - Indexes and Tables - Index/Table\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420	21			0	tr	In the \<emph\>Type \</emph\>box, select "Alphabetical Index".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154107	22			0	tr	In the \<emph\>Options \</emph\>area, select the \<emph\>Concordance file\</emph\> check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153668	23			0	tr	Click the \<emph\>File\</emph\> button, and then choose \<emph\>New\</emph\> or \<emph\>Edit\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154470	24			0	tr	A concordance file contains the following fields: 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152953	3			0	tr	"Search term" refers to the index entry that you want to mark in the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155896	4			0	tr	"Alternative entry" refers to the index entry that you want to appear in the index.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3154194	5			0	tr	The 1st and 2nd Keys are parent index entries. The "Search term" or the "Alternative entry" appears as a subentry under the 1st and 2nd Keys.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155184	6			0	tr	"Match case" means that uppercase and lowercase letters are considered.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3143282	7			0	tr	"Word only" searches for the term as a single word.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3147220	8			0	tr	To enable the "Match case" or "Word only" options, click in the corresponding cell, and then select the check box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153629	25			0	tr	To create a concordance file without the Edit Concordance File dialog:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153644	9			0	tr	Use the following format guidelines when you create a concordance file:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3152770	10			0	tr	Each entry in the concordance file is on a separate line.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155142	26			0	tr	Commented lines start with #.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3153354	11			0	tr	Use the following format for the entries:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3149172	12			0	tr	Search term;Alternative entry;1st key;2nd key;Match case;Word only				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3156270	13			0	tr	The entries "Match case" and "Word only" are interpreted as "No" or FALSE if they are empty or zero (0). All other contents are interpreted as "Yes" or TRUE.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145778	27			0	tr	Örnek				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155907	14			0	tr	For example, to include the word "Boston" in your alphabetical index under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line in the concordance file:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151370	15			0	tr	Boston;Boston;Cities;;0;0 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3151383	16			0	tr	This also finds "Boston" if it is written in lowercase letters.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3155866	17			0	tr	To include the "Beacon Hill" district in Boston under the "Cities" entry, enter the following line:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120250.xhp	0	help	par_id3150116	18			0	tr	Beacon Hill;Boston;Cities; 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120300.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Kaynakça girişi ekle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\swriter\01\04120300.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151187	1			0	tr	Kaynakça girişi ekle				20130618 17:22:18
