helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150792				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>gradients; applying and defining\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>editing;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>defining;gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>custom gradients\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>transparency;adjusting\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150792	3			0	tr	\<variable id=\"gradient\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/gradient.xhp\" name=\"Creating Gradient Fills\"\>Creating Gradient Fills\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154012	4			0	tr	A gradient fill is an incremental blend of two different colors, or shades of the same color, that you can apply to a drawing object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147436	61			0	tr	To apply a gradient:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3146974	5			0	tr	Select a drawing object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154491	6			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and select \<emph\>Gradient\</emph\> as the \<emph\>Fill\</emph\> type.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3153415	7			0	tr	Select a gradient style from the list and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154702	8			0	tr	Creating Custom Gradients				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145791	9			0	tr	You can define your own gradients and modify existing gradients, as well as save and load a list of gradient files.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145384	62			0	tr	To create a custom gradient:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3151242	11			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150046	12			0	tr	Select a gradient from the list to use as the basis for your new gradient and click \<emph\>Add\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145116	13			0	tr	Type a name for the gradient in the text box and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id6535843				0	tr	The name appears at the end of the gradient list and is selected for editing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	15			0	tr	Set the gradient properties and click \<emph\>Modify\</emph\> to save the gradient.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3156396	16			0	tr	Click \<emph\>OK.\</emph\> 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149947	40			0	tr	Using Gradients and Transparency				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3157905	41			0	tr	You can adjust the properties of a gradient as well as the transparency of a drawing object with your mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150653	63			0	tr	To adjust the gradient of a drawing object:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3154844	42			0	tr	Select a drawing object with the gradient that you want to modify.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3145592	43			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Gradients\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_idN107BE				0	tr	Adjust the values for the gradient to suit your needs and click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\gradient.xhp	0	help	par_id3150659	46			0	tr	To adjust the transparency of an object, select the object, choose \<emph\>Format - Area\</emph\> and click the \<emph\>Transparency\</emph\> tab.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Inserting Graphics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3156443				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>pictures; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>images; inserting\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>files; inserting pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156443	1			0	tr	\<variable id=\"graphic_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/graphic_insert.xhp\" name=\"Inserting Graphics\"\>Inserting Pictures\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155600	2			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Picture - From File\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	3			0	tr	Locate the picture you want to insert. Select the \<emph\>Link\</emph\> check box to insert only a link to the picture. If you want to see the picture before you insert it, select \<emph\>Preview\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155764	4			0	tr	After you insert a linked picture, do not change the name of the source picture or move the source picture to another directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\graphic_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150044	5			0	tr	Click \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to insert the picture.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Nesneleri Grupla				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150793				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>grouping; draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects; grouping\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150793	26			0	tr	\<variable id=\"groups\"\>\<link href=\"text/sdraw/guide/groups.xhp\" name=\"Grouping Objects\"\>Grouping Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3153728	27			0	tr	You can combine several objects into a group so that they act as a single object. You can move and transform all objects in a group as a single unit. You can also change the properties (for example, line size, fill color) of all objects in a group as a whole or for individual objects in a group. Groups can be temporary or assigned:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147434	64			0	tr	Temporary - group only lasts as long as all of the combined objects are selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3154490	65			0	tr	Assigned - group lasts until it is ungrouped through a menu command.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	66			0	tr	Groups can also be grouped in other groups. Actions applied to a group do not affect the relative position of the individual objects to each other in the group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150716	28			0	tr	To group objects:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3149018				0	tr	\<image id=\"img_id3145643\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_formatgroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3145643\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147346	29			0	tr	Select the objects you want to group and choose \<emph\>Modify - Group\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3148485	30			0	tr	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3147002	31			0	tr	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150205	55			0	tr	Selecting Objects in a Group				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150370				0	tr	\<image id=\"img_id3155376\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_entergroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155376\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3156450	56			0	tr	You can select single objects in a group by entering the group. Double-click a group to enter it and click on the object to select it. You can also add or delete objects to and from a group in this mode. The objects that are not part of the group are grayed out.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3151239				0	tr	\<image id=\"img_id3155264\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_leavegroup.png\" width=\"0.1665inch\" height=\"0.1665inch\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155264\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id3150213	58			0	tr	To exit a group, double-click anywhere outside it.				20130618 17:22:18
