helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750	46			0	tr	There are several types of text you can add to a drawing or presentation: 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10824				0	tr	Text in a text box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10828				0	tr	Text that changes character size to fill the frame size				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN1082C				0	tr	Text that is added to any drawing object by double-clicking the object				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10830				0	tr	Text that is copied from a Writer document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN10834				0	tr	Text that is inserted from a text document or HTML document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150202	48			0	tr	Adding a Text Box				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3155266	49			0	tr	Click the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> icon \<image id=\"img_id3156450\" src=\"res/commandimagelist/sc_text.png\" width=\"0.1665in\" height=\"0.1665in\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3156450\"\>Icon\</alt\>\</image\> and move the mouse pointer to where you want to enter the text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3149052	50			0	tr	Drag a text box to the size you want in your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3151194	51			0	tr	Type or paste your text into the text box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118	53			0	tr	Double-click the text to edit it or to format text properties, such as font size or font color. Click the border of the text box to edit the object properties, such as border color or arranging in front or behind other objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150437	54			0	tr	Fitting Text to Frames				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id3146877	56			0	tr	Create a text box as described in the steps above.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108A3				0	tr	With the text object selected, choose \<emph\>Format - Text\</emph\>. The \<emph\>Text\</emph\> dialog opens.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_idN108AF				0	tr	On the \<emph\>Text\</emph\> tab page, clear the \<emph\>Fit height to text\</emph\> checkbox, then select the \<emph\>Fit to frame\</emph\> checkbox. Click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sdraw\guide\text_enter.xhp	0	help	par_id0610200902133994				0	tr	Now you can resize the text box to change the size and shape of the text characters.				20130618 17:22:18
