helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	4			0	tr	Open FileName As String [For Mode] [Access IOMode] [Protected] As [#]FileNumber As Integer [Len = DatasetLength]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280	5			0	tr	Parametreler:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	6			0	tr	\<emph\>FileName: \</emph\>Name and path of the file that you wan to open. If you try to read a file that does not exist (Access = Read), an error message appears. If you try to write to a file that does not exist (Access = Write), a new file is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262	7			0	tr	\<emph\>Mode:\</emph\> Keyword that specifies the file mode. Valid values: Append (append to sequential file), Binary (data can be accessed by bytes using Get and Put), Input (opens data channel for reading), Output (opens data channel for writing), and Random (edits relative files).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3154014	8			0	tr	\<emph\>IOMode:\</emph\> Keyword that defines the access type. Valid values: Read (read-only), Write (write-only), Read Write (both).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3150011	9			0	tr	\<emph\>Protected:\</emph\> Keyword that defines the security status of a file after opening. Valid values: Shared (file may be opened by other applications), Lock Read (file is protected against reading), Lock Write (file is protected against writing), Lock Read Write (denies file access).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153190	10			0	tr	\<emph\>FileNumber:\</emph\> Any integer expression from 0 to 511 to indicate the number of a free data channel. You can then pass commands through the data channel to access the file. The file number must be determined by the FreeFile function immediately before the Open statement.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3151115	11			0	tr	\<emph\>DatasetLength:\</emph\> For random access files, set the length of the records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03020103.xhp	0	help	par_id3153418	12			0	tr	You can only modify the contents of a file that was opened with the Open statement. If you try to open a file that is already open, an error message appears.				20130618 17:22:18
