helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3154124	8			0	tr	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> Numeric expression that contains the serial time number that is used to calculate the number of seconds.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	9			0	tr	This function is the opposite of the \<emph\>TimeSerial \</emph\>function. It returns the seconds of a serial time value that is generated by the \<emph\>TimeSerial\</emph\> or \<emph\>TimeValue \</emph\>functions. For example, the expression:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3153951	10			0	tr	Print Second(TimeSerial(12,30,41))				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03030204.xhp	0	help	par_id3151117	11			0	tr	returns the value 41.				20130618 17:22:18
