helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03120104.xhp	0	help	par_id3149670	9			0	tr	Using the Val function, you can convert a string that represents numbers into numeric expressions. This is the inverse of the \<emph\>Str\</emph\> function. If only part of the string contains numbers, only the first appropriate characters of the string are converted. If the string does not contain any numbers, the \<emph\>Val\</emph\> function returns the value 0.				20130618 17:22:18
