helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3150342	11			0	tr	A curved line segment consists of two data points (endpoints) and two control points (handles). A control line connects a control point to a data point. You can change the shape of a curve by converting a data point to a different type, or by dragging the control points to a different location.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\line_edit.xhp	0	help	par_id3145252	16			0	tr	You can also modify the properties of the line by selecting the line and choosing \<emph\>Format - Line\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
