helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id4901272				0	tr	\<variable id=\"show\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/show.xhp\" name=\"Showing a Slide Show\"\>Showing a Slide Show\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9636829				0	tr	Different ways exist to start a slide show. Once a slide show is running, you can take control pressing keys or clicking the mouse buttons.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id7076937				0	tr	By default, a slide show always starts with the first slide. You advance manually through slides up to the last slide. You can change these settings.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id9954527				0	tr	Running a Slide Show				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6860255				0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show\</emph\> to run the show.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4199957				0	tr	If you want all shows to start from the current slide instead of the first slide, choose \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Impress - General\</emph\> and click \<emph\>Always with current page\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3209936				0	tr	Click to advance to the next effect or to the next slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8702658				0	tr	Press \<item type=\"keycode\"\>Esc\</item\> to abort the show before the end.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3741264				0	tr	Many more keys are available to \<link href=\"text/simpress/04/01020000.xhp\"\>control a slide show\</link\>. You can also right-click to open a context menu with useful commands.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id5694143				0	tr	Showing an automatic slide show (kiosk mode)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id5829645				0	tr	For an automatic change to the next slide, you must assign a slide transition to each slide. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id2361522				0	tr	On the Task Pane, click \<emph\>Slide Transition\</emph\> to open that tab page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9168980				0	tr	In the \<emph\>Advance slide\</emph\> area, click \<emph\>Automatically after\</emph\>, and select a time duration.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9766533				0	tr	Click \<emph\>Apply to All Slides\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id6081728				0	tr	You can assign a different time for every slide to advance to the next slide. The \<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/rehearse_timings.xhp\"\>rehearse timings\</link\> feature can assist you to get the timing right.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id9219641				0	tr	To advance to the first slide, after all slides have been shown, you must set the slide show to repeat automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id3174230				0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Slide Show - Slide Show Settings\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1336405				0	tr	In the Type area, click \<emph\>Auto\</emph\> and select a pause time between shows.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4959257				0	tr	When you create a new slide show using the \<link href=\"text/shared/autopi/01050000.xhp\"\>Presentation Wizard\</link\>, you can select the duration of slides and of the pause, on the third wizard page.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	hd_id1906491				0	tr	Running a slide show from a file				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id4799340				0	tr	You can start %PRODUCTNAME from a command prompt, followed by the parameter \<item type=\"literal\"\>-show\</item\> and an Impress filename. For example, to start the file \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> from the command prompt, enter the following command:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id1502121				0	tr	\<item type=\"literal\"\>soffice -show filename.odp\</item\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\show.xhp	0	help	par_id8266853				0	tr	This assumes that soffice is in the program path of your system, and that \<item type=\"literal\"\>filename.odp\</item\> is located in the current directory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Including Spreadsheets in Slides				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154022				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>spreadsheets;in presentations\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>presentations;inserting spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>including spreadsheets\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154022	1			0	tr	\<variable id=\"table_insert\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/table_insert.xhp\" name=\"Including Spreadsheets in Slides\"\>Including Spreadsheets in Slides\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id4231086				0	tr	You can apply different methods to insert spreadsheet cells into your Impress slides or Draw pages:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id9209875				0	tr	Insert a native table - you enter the data into the cells and apply fancy formatting using the Table Design section on the Tasks pane.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3044526				0	tr	Insert a new table as an OLE object or insert an existing file as an OLE object - you can specify the link to a file to be a live link to the latest data saved in a spreadsheet file.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id137333				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of columns for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8626667				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Enter the number of rows for the new table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551581				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Define the vertical alignment of selected or all cell contents. Split or merge cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551553				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All selected cells are merged into one cell.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551535				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The selected cell is split into several cells. You see the Split Cells dialog box.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551651				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are align at the top of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551697				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned vertically centered in the cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551632				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The cell contents are aligned at the bottom of the cells.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_idN10626				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Selects the current table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551734				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all rows.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080035				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the height of the selected or all rows to the same size. The height of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080063				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all rows will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all rows containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080408008				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new row will be inserted at the bottom of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new rows as the selection has will be inserted below the selection.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804080050				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All rows of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163012				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Choose commands for the selected or all columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163092				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Distributes the width of the selected or all columns to the same size. The width of the table is not changed.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163046				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, all columns will be selected. If currently cells are selected, all columns containing the selected cells will be selected.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163128				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>If currently no cell is selected, a new column will be inserted at the right border of the table. If currently cells are selected, as many new columns as the selection has will be inserted right of the selection.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163127				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>All columns of the current selection will be deleted.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200804163151				0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\".\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Align the table within the page or slide.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id8594317				0	tr	Inserting a native table				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id7184972				0	tr	Go to the Impress slide or Draw page where you want to insert the table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id248115				0	tr	Choose \<item type=\"menuitem\"\>Insert - Table\</item\> or use the Table icon on the Standard toolbar to insert a table.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2748496				0	tr	Double-click the table and enter or paste the data into the cells. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id8270210				0	tr	Select some cell contents and right-click to open the context menu. Choose commands to change the cell's contents, like font size and line spacing.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id6820276				0	tr	Right-click the table border to open the table's context menu. Use the table's context menu to enter a name and description for the table, or to distribute the rows or columns equally, among other commands.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551725				0	tr	Select some cells and right-click to open a context menu, where you can insert or delete rows and columns, among other commands. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id091620080355171				0	tr	To select a rectangular area of cells, point to a cell in one corner of the rectangle, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the opposite corner of the rectangle, then release the mouse button. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id0916200803551880				0	tr	To select one cell, point to that cell, hold down the mouse button, and drag the mouse to the next cell and back, then release the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151075	2			0	tr	Inserting a new spreadsheet as an OLE object				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150715	7			0	tr	You can add a blank $[officename] Calc spreadsheet to a slide as an OLE object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150749	3			0	tr	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3146313	18			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - OLE- Object\</emph\>. Click \<emph\>Create new\</emph\> and select the %PRODUCTNAME Spreadsheet. Click OK. Click in the spreadsheet to enter your data. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id2466505				0	tr	Click outside the spreadsheet to view the slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3148870	9			0	tr	To resize the spreadsheet without resizing the cells, double-click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle. To resize the cells of the spreadsheet, click the spreadsheet, and then drag a corner handle.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150215	11			0	tr	Inserting a spreadsheet from a file				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154765	19			0	tr	When you insert an existing spreadsheet into your slide, changes that are made to the original spreadsheet file are not updated on your slide. You can, however, make changes to the spreadsheet in your slide.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3145112	12			0	tr	Go to the slide where you want to insert the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3153075	13			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150391	14			0	tr	Select \<emph\>Create from file\</emph\>, and click \<emph\>Search\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150537	20			0	tr	Locate the file you want to insert, and then click\<emph\> OK\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id1616565				0	tr	Enable the \<emph\>Link to file\</emph\> checkbox to insert the file as a live link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3155256	21			0	tr	The entire spreadsheet is inserted into your slide. If you want to change the sheet that is displayed, double-click the spreadsheet, and then select a different sheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3154505	15			0	tr	\<link href=\"text/simpress/01/05130000.xhp\" name=\"Format - Slide Layout\"\>Format - Slide Layout\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\table_insert.xhp	0	help	par_id3150335	16			0	tr	\<link href=\"text/shared/01/04150100.xhp\" name=\"Insert - Object - OLE Object\"\>Insert - Object - OLE Object\</link\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150717				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>text; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>characters; converting to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>sign conversion to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; text to curves\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>curves;converting text to\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150717	3			0	tr	\<variable id=\"text2curve\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/text2curve.xhp\" name=\"Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\"\>Converting Text Characters into Drawing Objects\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3155960	21			0	tr	You can convert text characters into curves that you can edit and resize as you would any drawing object. Once you convert text into a drawing object, you can no longer edit the content of the text.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153965	22			0	tr	To convert text into a drawing object:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3146963	4			0	tr	Select the text that you want to convert, and do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3149053	5			0	tr	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150395	23			0	tr	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the border of the text object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Curve\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150746	6			0	tr	If your text contains more than one character, the converted text becomes a grouped object. Double-click the group to edit individual objects. Press Esc when finished.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\text2curve.xhp	0	help	par_id3150336	7			0	tr	Now, click the \<emph\>Points\</emph\> icon on the \<emph\>Drawing\</emph\> bar. Click the object. You can see all the Bézier points of the object. On the \<emph\>Edit Points\</emph\> bar, you can find various icons for editing, inserting and deleting points.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153415				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>vectorizing bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>converting; bitmaps to polygons\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>bitmaps; converting to vector graphics\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>vector graphics;converting bitmaps\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153415	26			0	tr	\<variable id=\"vectorize\"\>\<link href=\"text/simpress/guide/vectorize.xhp\" name=\"Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\"\>Converting Bitmap Images into Vector Graphics\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3155633	27			0	tr	A vector graphic can be resized without losing the quality of the graphic. In $[officename] Draw and Impress, you can convert a bitmap image into a vector graphic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151241	28			0	tr	Select the bitmap image that you want to convert.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3153812	29			0	tr	Do one of the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3145118	37			0	tr	In $[officename] Draw, choose \<emph\>Modify - Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3151387	38			0	tr	In $[officename] Impress, right-click the object, and then choose \<emph\>Convert - To Polygon\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\simpress\guide\vectorize.xhp	0	help	par_id3149349	30			0	tr	Set the conversion options for the image, and then click \<emph\>OK\</emph\>. See \<link href=\"text/simpress/01/13050200.xhp\" name=\"Convert to Polygon\"\>\<emph\>Convert to Polygon\</emph\>\</link\> for a description of the conversion options.				20130618 17:22:18
