helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	bm_id3147399				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>accessibility; $[officename] assistive technology\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>assistive technology in $[officename]\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen readers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>screen magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>magnifiers\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147399	22			0	tr	\<variable id=\"assistive\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/assistive.xhp\" name=\"Assistive Tools in $[officename]\"\>Assistive Tools in $[officename]\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	25			0	tr	$[officename] supports some assistive technology tools like screen magnification software, screen readers, and on-screen keyboards. Most of these tools communicate with $[officename] by means of the Java(TM) Access Bridge software, that uses the Java Accessibility API, a part of the Java runtime environment.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id8847010				0	tr	A current list of supported assistive tools can be found on the Apache OpenOffice Wiki at \<link href=\"http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\"\>http://wiki.services.openoffice.org/wiki/Accessibility\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345	12			0	tr	Requirements to use assistive tools in $[officename]				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3147209	13			0	tr	Java Runtime Environment (JRE) version 1.4.1_01 and higher, or version 1.4.0_02 with the locale set to "en_us".				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3146797	26			0	tr	Most recent version of the software for your assistive tool				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	15			0	tr	On Windows systems, \<link href=\"http://www.sun.com/access/downloads/\" name=\"Java Access Bridge\"\>Java Access Bridge\</link\> software version 1.0.3 or higher 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	16			0	tr	On UNIX(R) systems, the GNOME 2 desktop environment with the Java Access Bridge software for GNOME				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149795	23			0	tr	Supported Assistive Tools				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155419	2			0	tr	On Windows systems, $[officename] directly supports most on-screen keyboard software. Additional support for assistive tools is provided by the Java Access Bridge software. The following is a list of some assistive tools that use the Java Access Bridge software to exchange data with $[officename]:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156329	4			0	tr	ZoomText Screen Magnifier (version 7.11 or higher)(Windows)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	5			0	tr	Gnopernicus Screen Reader and Magnifier, using GNOME Assistive Technology Service Provider Interface (at-spi) and Java Accessibility API software				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3148474	6			0	tr	GNOME On Screen Keyboard (GOK), using GNOME at-spi and Java Accessibility API software				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153061	24			0	tr	Supported Input Devices				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3156024	7			0	tr	$[officename] provides the ability to use alternative input devices for access to all functions of $[officename].				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149045	8			0	tr	Screen magnification software allow users with low vision to work in $[officename] with caret and focus tracking.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3152811	9			0	tr	On-screen keyboards enable users to perform almost all data input and commands with a mouse.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	10			0	tr	Screen readers allow visually impaired users to access $[officename] with text-to-speech and Braille displays.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\assistive.xhp	0	help	par_id3149808	11			0	tr	When accessibility support in $[officename] is enabled, the Java Runtime Environment is loaded, and increases the startup time for $[officename].				20130618 17:22:18
