helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151111	34			0	tr	A fast way of copying from a data source into a text or spreadsheet document, or of creating forms based on a data source, is by drag-and-drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3147335				0	tr	\<image id=\"img_id3155390\" src=\"res/helpimg/copydata.png\" width=\"8.47mm\" height=\"8.47mm\"\>\<alt id=\"alt_id3155390\"\>Mouse pointer copying data\</alt\>\</image\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3145315	35			0	tr	Copying with Drag-and-Drop				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149233	28			0	tr	If you want to reverse a drag-and-drop, position the cursor in your document and choose \<emph\>Edit - Undo\</emph\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149656	46			0	tr	It is also possible to copy by drag-and-drop from a document into a data source:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153379	47			0	tr	A text table or the selected range of a spreadsheet can be dragged using drag-and-drop to a table container in the data source explorer.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3151211	48			0	tr	Plain text can be copied using drag-and-drop from one document to a data field in the data source view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145421	36			0	tr	Using data in a text document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3154685	12			0	tr	You can insert a database field in a text document by dragging a field name from the column header of the data source view into the document. This is especially useful when designing form letters. Simply drag the desired fields - home address, form of address, and so on - into your document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3153105	37			0	tr	To insert a complete record, select the corresponding header and drag it into the document. When you release the mouse button, the \<link href=\"text/shared/02/12070000.xhp\" name=\"Insert database columns\"\>\<emph\>Insert database columns\</emph\>\</link\> dialog appears, in which you can decide whether to use all database fields, and whether to copy the data into the document as text, a table or fields. All currently selected records will be inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147230	39			0	tr	Applying data to a table document				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3125864	40			0	tr	You can insert one or more records into the current sheet of a spreadsheet by selecting the rows in the data source view and dragging and dropping them into the spreadsheet. The data is inserted at the place where you release the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149766	42			0	tr	Inserting controls in a text form				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3155132	43			0	tr	When you create a text form linked to a database, you can generate controls by drag-and-drop from the data source view.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_beamer.xhp	0	help	par_id3149562	45			0	tr	When you drag a database column into the text document, you insert a field. If you hold down Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> while dragging, a text field is inserted, grouped with an appropriate label field. The text field already contains all the database information that you need for the form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Copying Graphics From the Gallery				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3145345				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>Gallery;dragging pictures to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>draw objects;dropping Gallery pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;from Gallery to draw objects\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145345	40			0	tr	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_fromgallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics From the Gallery\"\>Copying Graphics From the Gallery\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3155535	41			0	tr	If you drag a graphic from the Gallery into a text, spreadsheet or presentation document, the graphic will be inserted there.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149762	45			0	tr	If you release the graphic \<emph\>directly on a draw object\</emph\>, please note the following:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153825	43			0	tr	If you move the graphic (drag it without pressing any key, in which case no additional symbol appears next to the mouse pointer), only the attributes are copied from the graphic and applied to the draw object on which you release the mouse button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	42			0	tr	If you copy the graphic (drag it while holding down the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, in which case a plus sign appears next to the mouse pointer), the graphic will be inserted as an object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_fromgallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154514	44			0	tr	If you create a hyperlink (drag while holding down Shift and \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>, in which case a linking arrow appears next to the mouse pointer), the drawing object is replaced by the graphic from the Gallery, but the position and size of the replaced draw object are retained.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Adding Graphics to the Gallery				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	bm_id3154927				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>Gallery; adding pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures;adding to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>inserting;pictures in Gallery\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;to Gallery\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154927	49			0	tr	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_gallery\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_gallery.xhp\" name=\"Adding Graphics to the Gallery\"\>Adding Graphics to the Gallery\</link\> \</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3143267	50			0	tr	You can place a graphic from a document such as an HTML page in the Gallery by drag-and-drop.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3154823	56			0	tr	Display the Gallery theme to which you want to add the graphic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3153748	51			0	tr	Position the mouse pointer above the graphic, without clicking.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	52			0	tr	If the mouse pointer changes to a hand symbol, the graphic refers to a hyperlink. In this case, click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key to select it without executing the respective link.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3149578	53			0	tr	If the mouse pointer does not change to a hand symbol, you can simply click the graphic to select it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3145120	54			0	tr	Once the graphic is selected, release the mouse button. Click again on the graphic image, keeping the mouse button pressed for more than two seconds. The graphic image is copied to the internal memory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_gallery.xhp	0	help	par_id3150772	55			0	tr	Without releasing the mouse button, drag the graphic into the Gallery.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Copying Graphics Between Documents				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	bm_id3159201				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>drag and drop; pictures\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pictures; drag and drop between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>copying;pictures, between documents\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>pasting;pictures from other documents\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159201	15			0	tr	\<variable id=\"dragdrop_graphic\"\>\<link href=\"text/shared/guide/dragdrop_graphic.xhp\" name=\"Copying Graphics Between Documents\"\>Copying Graphics Between Documents\</link\>\</variable\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155805	16			0	tr	You can copy a graphic from one document to another by drag-and-drop. If you plan to publish your document, please observe copyright laws and obtain the consent of the authors.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3147576	17			0	tr	Open the document in which you want to insert the graphic object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155338	18			0	tr	Open the document from which you want to copy the graphic.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149182	19			0	tr	Click the graphic while pressing the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> key, to select it without executing any hyperlinks it may refer to.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3151110	20			0	tr	Keep the mouse button pressed and wait a moment while the object is copied to an internal memory.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	21			0	tr	Drag the graphic into the other document. \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible side by side, first move the mouse pointer to the button of the target document while keeping the mouse button pressed. The document in question is then displayed and you can move the mouse pointer into the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3155628	22			0	tr	Release the mouse button as soon as the gray text cursor indicates the position where you want to insert a copy of the picture.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_graphic.xhp	0	help	par_id3150276	56			0	tr	If the graphic is connected with a hyperlink, the hyperlink and not the graphic is inserted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Copying Spreadsheet Areas to Text Documents				20130618 17:22:18
