helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155892	25			0	tr	Open both the text document and the spreadsheet.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3147088	26			0	tr	Select the sheet area you want to copy.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149827	27			0	tr	Point to the selected area and press the mouse button. Keep the mouse button pressed for a moment, then drag the area into the text document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3152780	32			0	tr	\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"WIN\"\>If the documents are not visible next to each other, first drag the mouse pointer to the destination document button. Continue to hold down the mouse button. The document is displayed, and you can move the mouse pointer within the document. \</caseinline\>\</switchinline\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3156346	28			0	tr	Once the cursor is located in the place where you want to insert the sheet area, release the mouse button. The sheet area is inserted as an OLE object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154047	29			0	tr	You can select and edit the OLE object at any time.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3149164	30			0	tr	To edit the OLE object, double-click on it.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3155389	33			0	tr	Alternatively, select the object and choose \<emph\>Edit - Object - Edit\</emph\> or choose \<emph\>Edit\</emph\> from the context menu. You edit the object in its own frame within the text document, but you see the icons and menu commands needed for spreadsheets.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\dragdrop_table.xhp	0	help	par_id3154860	31			0	tr	Choose \<emph\>Open\</emph\> to open the source document of the OLE object.				20130618 17:22:18
