helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id2307199				0	tr	You can combine several graphic objects into a group so that you can use them like a single object. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id9983825				0	tr	You can move, transform, resize, distort, or convert all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group any time to change the individual objects. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id5734733				0	tr	You can change the properties (line size, fill color, and more) of all objects in a group together, and you can enter the group and change the individual objects. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id561540				0	tr	Groups can also be nested to form groups within other groups. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	hd_id7705618				0	tr	To group objects				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id607013				0	tr	Select the objects together that you want to group. Hold down Shift while you click the individual objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1399578				0	tr	Right-click any of the selected objects to open the context menu. 				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id598162				0	tr	In Impress or Draw, choose Group. In Calc or Writer, choose Group – Group.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id6738792				0	tr	To select the objects, you can also drag a selection frame around the objects.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id7309793				0	tr	For example, you can group all of the objects in a company logo to move and resize the logo as a single object.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\groups.xhp	0	help	par_id1227759				0	tr	After you have grouped objects, selecting any part of the group selects the entire group.				20130618 17:22:18
