helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3148405	56			0	tr	Use the arrow keys to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3145619	57			0	tr	Set the grid resolution unit with \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - %PRODUCTNAME Writer - Grid\</emph\> in the \<emph\>Resolution\</emph\> area. If you enter a number greater than 1 in the \<emph\>Subdivision\</emph\> area, you must press the arrow key as often as the number states to move the selected object by one grid resolution unit.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3166450	58			0	tr	Use the \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Option\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Alt\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> and arrow keys to move the selected object by one pixel.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\keyboard.xhp	0	help	par_id3147345	59			0	tr	Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to enter the handle edit mode. The upper left handle is the active handle, it starts blinking. Use \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to select the next handle. Press Escape to exit the handle edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
