helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Special properties of a formatted field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150774				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>formatted fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>fields; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; formatted fields\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150774	131			0	tr	Special properties of a formatted field				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3156410	127			0	tr	\<emph\>Formatting\</emph\>: You can set the \<emph\>Formatting \</emph\>property by clicking the \<emph\>... \</emph\>button in the \<emph\>Formatting\</emph\> line of the \<emph\>Properties: Formatted Field\</emph\> dialog. The \<emph\>Number Format\</emph\> dialog appears.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150443	128			0	tr	If the formatted field is connected to the text field of a database, the entries in this field will be treated as text. If the formatted field is connected to a field of the database that can be displayed as a number, the input is treated as numbers. The date and time are also handled internally as numbers.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3150976	129			0	tr	\<emph\>Min. value\</emph\> and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>: You can enter the minimum and maximum numeric value for a formatted field. The min and max values determine the output of existing data (Example: Min. value is 5, the connected database field contains the integer value 3. The output is 5, but the value in the database is not modified) and the input of new data (Example: Max. value is 10 and you enter 20. The input is corrected and 10 is written in the database). If the fields are not filled in for \<emph\>Min. value \</emph\>and \<emph\>Max. value\</emph\>, no limits will be applied. For formatted fields that are connected to a database text field, these two values and the \<emph\>Default value\</emph\> do not apply.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170002.xhp	0	help	par_id3153665	130			0	tr	\<emph\>Default value\</emph\>: This value is set for new records as the default value.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Special Tips for Date Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	bm_id3150445				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>date fields; properties\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150445	77			0	tr	Special Tips for Date Fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3154230	75			0	tr	When you enter a year using two digits, the corresponding four digit value is determined by a setting in \<emph\>\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>%PRODUCTNAME - Preferences\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Tools - Options\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\> - $[officename] - General\</emph\>. For example, if 1935 is set as the lower limiting value and you enter 34 as a date value, then the result is 2034 instead of 1934.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170003.xhp	0	help	par_id3149205	76			0	tr	The pre-set limit value will be saved for each document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	tit				0	tr	Special Tips for Table Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	bm_id3109850				0	tr	\<bookmark_value\>table controls; properties\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>controls; properties of table controls\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>table controls;keyboard-only edit mode\</bookmark_value\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3109850	124			0	tr	Special Tips for Table Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153539	51			0	tr	You can define a table control to display the records as you like. In other words you can define data fields for displaying or editing data like in a database form.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152372	62			0	tr	The following fields are possible in a table control: text, date, time and currency field, numeric field, pattern field, check box and combo box. In the case of combined date/time fields, two columns are created automatically.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159194	125			0	tr	The number of selected lines, if any are selected, is in parentheses after the total number of records.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155616	52			0	tr	To insert columns into the table control, click in the column heads and bring up the context menu. The following commands are available:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150789	53			0	tr	Sütun Ekle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153750	54			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_INSERTCOL\"\>Calls a submenu to select a data field to adopt it in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3155552	59			0	tr	Configure the table control using drag and drop: Open the data source browser and drag the desired fields out of the data source browser and on to the column heads of the table control. A pre-configured column is created.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149827	55			0	tr	Yerine konulan:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3153345	56			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_CHANGECOL\"\>Opens a submenu to select a data field to replace the data field selected in the table control.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3143267	57			0	tr	Sütun Sil				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3157958	58			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_DELETECOL\"\>Deletes the currently selected column.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147275	73			0	tr	Sütun				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3152996	74			0	tr	Opens the properties dialog of the selected column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148539	79			0	tr	Hide Columns				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159157	80			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_HIDECOL\"\>Hides the selected column.\</ahelp\> Its properties are not changed.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150771	81			0	tr	Sütunları görüntüle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159400	82			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS\"\>Calls a submenu where you can select the columns to show again.\</ahelp\> To show only one column, click the column name. You see only the first 16 hidden columns. If there are more hidden columns, choose the \<emph\>More\</emph\> command to call the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156193	83			0	tr	Diğer				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3159269	84			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWCOLS_MORE\"\>Calls the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149763	85			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SVX:LISTBOX:RID_SVX_DLG_SHOWGRIDCOLUMNS:1\"\>In the \<emph\>Show Columns\</emph\> dialog you can select the columns to be shown. Hold down the Shift or Ctrl (Mac: Command) key to select multiple entries.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153561	86			0	tr	Tümü				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3150504	87			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SID_FM_SHOWALLCOLS\"\>Click \<emph\>All \</emph\>if you want to show all columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153349	127			0	tr	Keyboard-only control of Table Controls				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3149416	126			0	tr	If you use the keyboard only to travel through controls in your document, you will find one difference to the other types of controls: the Tab key does not move the cursor to the next control, but moves to the next column inside the table control. Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the next control, or press Shift+\<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Tab to move to the previous control.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153062	128			0	tr	To enter the special keyboard-only edit mode for Table Controls:				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3144510	129			0	tr	The form document must be in \<link href=\"text/shared/02/01170500.xhp\" name=\"design mode\"\>design mode\</link\>.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154758	130			0	tr	Press \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+F6 to select the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3161657	131			0	tr	Press Shift+F4 to select the first control. If the Table Control is not the first control, press Tab until it is selected.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3151056	132			0	tr	Press Enter to enter the edit mode. The handles are shown farther out from the control border.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154938	133			0	tr	In the edit mode, you can open the edit mode context menu by pressing Shift+F10.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3154365	134			0	tr	If you want to edit columns, press Shift+Space to enter column edit mode. Now you can rearrange the order of columns with \<switchinline select=\"sys\"\>\<caseinline select=\"MAC\"\>Command\</caseinline\>\<defaultinline\>Ctrl\</defaultinline\>\</switchinline\>+Arrow keys. The Delete key deletes the current column.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170004.xhp	0	help	par_id3145419	135			0	tr	Press the Escape key to exit the edit mode.				20130618 17:22:18
