helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3154681	145			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_PROP_DEFAULT_BUTTON\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key.\</ahelp\>The\<emph\> Default button\</emph\> property specifies that the corresponding button will be operated when you press the Return key. If you open the dialog or form and do not carry out any further action, the button with this property is the default button.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3149750	175			0	tr	This property should be assigned only to a single button within the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\01170101.xhp	0	help	par_id3150931	177			0	tr	When using Web page forms, you might come across this property in search masks. These are edit masks that contain a text field and a Submit type button. The search term is entered in the text field and the search is started by activating the button. If the button is defined as the default button, however, simply hit Enter after entering the search term in order to start the search.				20130618 17:22:18
