helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154380	30			0	tr	Specifies the format for inserting the database fields into the document.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156329	14			0	tr	Veritabanından				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149415	31			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_DBFMT_FROM_DB\"\>Accepts the database formats.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159148	15			0	tr	Seçim				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152349	32			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:LISTBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:LB_DBFMT_FROM_USR\"\>Specifies a format from the list, if the format information of certain data fields is not accepted.\</ahelp\> The formats supplied here are only available for certain database fields, such as numeric or Boolean fields. If you select a database field in text format, you will not be able to select any format from the selection list, since the text format will be automatically maintained.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3144511	33			0	tr	If the format you want is not listed, select "Other Formats..." and define the desired format in the \<link href=\"text/shared/01/05020300.xhp\" name=\"Number Format\"\>\<emph\>Number Format\</emph\>\</link\> dialog.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154282	34			0	tr	The number format assigned using the selection list always refers to the database field selected in the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3154138	35			0	tr	To insert the data into the document in the form of a table, the correct \<emph\>Table\</emph\> option must be active. You can then select a database field from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box to define the formatting of the database field. The changes to the number formats will be applied to the last selection. It does not matter whether the database field was selected from the \<emph\>Database columns\</emph\> list box or from the \<emph\>Table column(s)\</emph\> list box.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3156280	10			0	tr	Tablo başlığı ekle				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150497	27			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:CHECKBOX:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:CB_TABLE_HEADON\"\>Specifies whether to insert a heading line for the columns in the text table.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153178	11			0	tr	Apply column name				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12070100.xhp	0	help	par_id3152922	28			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"SW:RADIOBUTTON:DLG_AP_INSERT_DB_SEL:RB_HEADL_COLNMS\"\>Uses the field names of the database table as headings for each of the text table columns.\</ahelp\>				20130618 17:22:18
