helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3155582	66			0	tr	"M*er" returns all entries starting with an "M" and ending in "er" (for example, Miller, Moller, Mather)				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3145762	48			0	tr	If you want to search for the actual characters ? or *, preface them with a backslash: "\\?" or "\\*". However, this is only necessary when \<emph\>Wildcard expression\</emph\> is enabled. When the option is not enabled, the wildcard characters are processed like normal characters.				20130618 17:22:18
