helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154477	102			0	tr	The \<emph\>State\</emph\> line shows the records returned by the search. If the search reaches the end (or the beginning) of a table, the search is automatically continued at the other end.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3163720	103			0	tr	In very large databases, finding the record in reverse search order can take some time. In this case, the status bar informs you that the records are still being counted.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147389	51			0	tr	Search / Cancel				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\02\12100200.xhp	0	help	par_id3154368	52			0	tr	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_SEARCH_BTN_SEARCH\" visibility=\"hidden\"\>Starts or cancels the search.\</ahelp\> If the search is successfully completed, the corresponding field in the table is highlighted. You can continue the search by clicking the \<emph\>Search\</emph\> button again. You can cancel a search process by clicking the \<emph\>Cancel\</emph\> button.				20130618 17:22:18
