helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3156130	79			0	tr	... the data field contains the indicated expression. The (*) placeholder indicates whether the expression x occurs at the beginning of (x*), at the end of (*x) or inside the field content (*x*). You can enter as a placeholder in SQL queries either the SQL % character or the familiar (*) file system placeholder in the $[officename] interface.				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150271	80			0	tr	The * or % placeholder stands for any number of characters. The question mark (?) in the $[officename] interface or the underscore (_) in SQL queries is used to represent exactly one character.				20130618 17:22:18
