helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153674	109			0	tr	Querying text fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3149134	110			0	tr	To query the content of a text field, you must put the expression between single quotes. The distinction between uppercase and lowercase letters depends on the database in use. LIKE, by definition, is case-sensitive (though some databases don't see it that strict).				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149302	111			0	tr	Querying date fields				20130618 17:22:18
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\explorer\database\02010100.xhp	0	help	par_id3150510	112			0	tr	Even if you want to filter by a date, you must place the expression between single quotation marks. The following formats are valid: YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS and YYYY/MM/DD HH:MM:SS as well as YYYY.MM.DD HH:MM:SS				20130618 17:22:18
